{"id":"272415f46291f82d","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-cor-birkhoff-limit.md","title":"Birkhoff Limit Properties","display":"cor-birkhoff-limit — Birkhoff Limit Properties","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-birkhoff-limit","aliases":["58-cor-birkhoff-limit"],"display":"cor-birkhoff-limit — Birkhoff Limit Properties","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-thm-birkhoff.md]]","[[58-df-probability-space]]","[[58-df-invariant-measure]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-birkhoff-limit"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-birkhoff-limit</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-birkhoff-limit — Birkhoff Limit Properties"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"8160ac3d14bcbf65\" href=\"?note=8160ac3d14bcbf65\" title=\"../batch12/58-thm-birkhoff.md\">../batch12/58-thm-birkhoff.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space\">58-df-probability-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"56239458358186f6\" href=\"?note=56239458358186f6\" title=\"58-df-invariant-measure\">58-df-invariant-measure</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\">\\((X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\)</span> (probability space, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space\">58-df-probability-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T:X\\to X\">\\(T:X\\to X\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>-measurable, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span>-preserving transformation, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"56239458358186f6\" href=\"?note=56239458358186f6\" title=\"58-df-invariant-measure\">58-df-invariant-measure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S\\)</span> (invariant-measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"56239458358186f6\" href=\"?note=56239458358186f6\" title=\"58-df-invariant-measure\">58-df-invariant-measure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in L^1(\\mu)\">\\(f\\in L^1(\\mu)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f^*:X\\to\\mathbb R\">\\(f^*:X\\to\\mathbb R\\)</span> (almost-everywhere limit of the ergodic averages)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}birkhoff\\text{-}limit}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\n\\land\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\n\\land f\\in L^1(\\mu)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land f^*\\in\\mathbb R^X\n\\land\\mu\\!\\left(X\\setminus\n\\left\\{x\\in X:f^*(x)=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac1n\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(T^i(x))\\right\\}\n\\right)=0\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\nf^*\\in L^1(\\mu)\n\\land\\mu\\!\\left(X\\setminus\\{x\\in X:f^*(T(x))=f^*(x)\\}\\right)=0\n\\land\\int_X f^*\\,d\\mu=\\int_X f\\,d\\mu.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}birkhoff\\text{-}limit}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\n\\land\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\n\\land f\\in L^1(\\mu)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land f^*\\in\\mathbb R^X\n\\land\\mu\\!\\left(X\\setminus\n\\left\\{x\\in X:f^*(x)=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac1n\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(T^i(x))\\right\\}\n\\right)=0\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\nf^*\\in L^1(\\mu)\n\\land\\mu\\!\\left(X\\setminus\\{x\\in X:f^*(T(x))=f^*(x)\\}\\right)=0\n\\land\\int_X f^*\\,d\\mu=\\int_X f\\,d\\mu.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The Birkhoff limit is integrable and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>-invariant almost everywhere.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> is ergodic, then <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f^*\">\\(f^*\\)</span> is almost everywhere the constant <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int_X f\\,d\\mu\">\\(\\int_X f\\,d\\mu\\)</span>; it need not equal <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-thm-birkhoff.md","status":"resolved","id":"8160ac3d14bcbf65","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-thm-birkhoff.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability-space","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-probability-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-invariant-measure","status":"resolved","id":"56239458358186f6","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-invariant-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability-space","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$ (probability space, see [[58-df-probability-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-invariant-measure","status":"resolved","id":"56239458358186f6","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$T:X\\to X$ ($\\Sigma$-measurable, $\\mu$-preserving transformation, see [[58-df-invariant-measure]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-invariant-measure","status":"resolved","id":"56239458358186f6","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S$ (invariant-measure predicate, see [[58-df-invariant-measure]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)","display":false},{"tex":"T:X\\to X","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"f\\in L^1(\\mu)","display":false},{"tex":"f^*:X\\to\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}birkhoff\\text{-}limit}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\n\\land\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\n\\land f\\in L^1(\\mu)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land f^*\\in\\mathbb R^X\n\\land\\mu\\!\\left(X\\setminus\n\\left\\{x\\in X:f^*(x)=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac1n\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(T^i(x))\\right\\}\n\\right)=0\n\\Bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad\\to\nf^*\\in L^1(\\mu)\n\\land\\mu\\!\\left(X\\setminus\\{x\\in X:f^*(T(x))=f^*(x)\\}\\right)=0\n\\land\\int_X f^*\\,d\\mu=\\int_X f\\,d\\mu.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"f^*","display":false},{"tex":"\\int_X f\\,d\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"f","display":false}],"bytes":1458,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-29","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-cor-birkhoff-limit.md|58-cor-birkhoff-limit]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["8160ac3d14bcbf65","0578a357a86e9d8f","56239458358186f6"]}